  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "On the roof, Chef Barinov tells Fedya to bring the inspector down—and explicitly adds that it is not a hint to throw him off. Naturally, Fedya takes that as a double hint and pushes the inspector over the edge just as police arrive.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, он сейчас на крыше!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, теперь спускай его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Подожди, это совсем не намёк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты просто спусти его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сбрасывать с крыши не надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, да я всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты что наделал сейчас, Федя?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Вы сказали спустить его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я сразу понял этот намёк.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, я сегодня пораньше уйду?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Потом меня в розыск объявят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "За что ты меня наказываешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это не я, он упал!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, он сейчас на крыше!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, he is on the roof right now!' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Chef Barinov' before landing on 'roof'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, теперь спускай его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Great, now bring him down.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'perfectly' and 'now' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Подожди, это совсем не намёк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, this is not a hint at all!' The meaning hinges on 'wait' working together with 'hint' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты просто спусти его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You just bring him downstairs.' Chef Barinov addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'downstairs'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сбрасывать с крыши не надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There is no need to throw him off the roof.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'to throw down' and 'with' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, да я всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, yes, I understood everything.' In Russian, the idea of 'Chef Barinov' flows naturally into 'understood' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты что наделал сейчас, Федя?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What have you done right now, Fedya?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'Fedya'. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Вы сказали спустить его вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You said to bring him down.' The plural past ending '-li' on the verb for 'told' covers a group or the polite 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я сразу понял этот намёк.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I immediately understood that hint.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'hint' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, я сегодня пораньше уйду?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, may I leave a bit early today?' Notice how Russian expresses 'Chef Barinov' and 'will leave' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Потом меня в розыск объявят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Later they will put me on the wanted list.' Fedya anchors the line on 'then', while 'to announce' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "За что ты меня наказываешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you punishing me for?' Chef Barinov addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'you punish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это не я, он упал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It was not me, he fell!' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'this' and 'not' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
